<title>SWITZERLAND: SBC  SAYS H1 PROVISIONS MORE THAN PLANNED.</title>
<headline>SBC  SAYS H1 PROVISIONS MORE THAN PLANNED.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss Bank Corp (SBC) said actual provisions in the first six months of 1997 were 98 million Swiss francs higher than a budgeted level of 325 million, which was based on a new risk accounting system.</p>
<p>SBC said in a statement that the difference of 98 million francs had been charged against a reserve of 2.080 billion Swiss francs set aside last year.</p>
</text>
